  "recordedAt": "2026-03-12T13:00:00Z",
  "contextText": "Reviewing the first clickable intake prototype with Corvid.",
  "hasTranscript": true,
  "speakers": [
    {
      "id": "m10-spk-a",
      "label": "A",
      "displayName": "Alex Rivera"
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-spk-b",
      "label": "B",
      "displayName": "Elif Kaya"
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-spk-c",
      "label": "C",
      "displayName": "Nadia Brooks"
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-spk-d",
      "label": "D",
      "displayName": "Samir Haddad"
    }
  ],
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m10-s001",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 7060,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks everyone. Nadia's going to walk us through the first clickable prototype of the new intake flow."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s002",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-c",
      "startMs": 7310,
      "endMs": 14750,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "So the big change is that allergies and current medication are now required and come first, not last."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s003",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-d",
      "startMs": 15000,
      "endMs": 19400,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "That alone would save my nurses a lot of chasing."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s004",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-b",
      "startMs": 19650,
      "endMs": 23670,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "How long does it take a patient to complete?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s005",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-c",
      "startMs": 23920,
      "endMs": 29080,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "In our internal tests, about four minutes. The paper form averages seven."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s006",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-b",
      "startMs": 29330,
      "endMs": 37150,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Our walk-in clinics see about 300 patients a day across the network, so three minutes each adds up fast."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s007",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-d",
      "startMs": 37400,
      "endMs": 44080,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The buttons feel small though. A lot of our patients are elderly, and some have tremors."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s008",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-c",
      "startMs": 44330,
      "endMs": 49870,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "That's fair. I'll revise the prototype with larger touch targets by next Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s009",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-a",
      "startMs": 50120,
      "endMs": 53380,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Should we keep the paper fallback form?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s010",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-b",
      "startMs": 53630,
      "endMs": 58790,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'd drop it. If we keep paper, staff will default to it."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s011",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-d",
      "startMs": 59040,
      "endMs": 64200,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'm nervous about that, but I agree the habit is the risk."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s012",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-b",
      "startMs": 64450,
      "endMs": 70370,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Then let's decide it. We drop the paper fallback form for the walk-in clinics."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s013",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-a",
      "startMs": 70620,
      "endMs": 74260,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Okay, decided. What about testing with real staff?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s014",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-b",
      "startMs": 74510,
      "endMs": 79290,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll recruit five front-desk staff for usability tests in three weeks."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s015",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-c",
      "startMs": 79540,
      "endMs": 82800,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Five is perfect for a first round."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s016",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-a",
      "startMs": 83050,
      "endMs": 86690,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Samir, how are you feeling, by the way?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s017",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-d",
      "startMs": 86940,
      "endMs": 90580,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Much better, thanks, back to nearly full hours."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s018",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-a",
      "startMs": 90830,
      "endMs": 95990,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Glad to hear it. Elif, when's the best time for the tests?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s019",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-b",
      "startMs": 96240,
      "endMs": 101780,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Mornings, before clinic hours. I always prefer morning meetings, the afternoons are chaos."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s020",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-c",
      "startMs": 102030,
      "endMs": 104530,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Morning sessions work for me."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s021",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-a",
      "startMs": 104780,
      "endMs": 107660,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Any accessibility requirements beyond touch targets?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s022",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-d",
      "startMs": 107910,
      "endMs": 111930,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "High contrast mode. Some clinics have very bright windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s023",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-c",
      "startMs": 112180,
      "endMs": 116580,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Noted, I'll add a high contrast theme to the backlog."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10-s024",
      "speakerId": "m10-spk-a",
      "startMs": 116830,
      "endMs": 123510,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Great. So: larger targets by next Tuesday, no paper fallback, and five testers in three weeks."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Corvid intake prototype review\n\n**Date:** March 12\n**Attendees:** Alex Rivera (Larkspur Labs), Nadia Brooks (Larkspur Labs), Elif Kaya (Corvid Health), Samir Haddad (Corvid Health)\n\n## Summary\n\nNadia walked the group through the first clickable prototype of the new patient intake flow for the Corvid Health walk-in clinics.\n\n## Prototype\n\n- Allergies and current medication are now required and come first rather than last. Samir expects this alone to save nurses a lot of chasing.\n- Completion takes about four minutes in internal tests, against an average of seven on the paper form.\n- Corvid's walk-in clinics see about 300 patients a day across the network, so the time saving compounds quickly.\n\n## Feedback\n\n- Buttons are too small for many elderly patients, some of whom have tremors.\n- A high contrast mode is needed because some clinics have very bright windows.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Drop the paper fallback form** for the walk-in clinics. Elif's reasoning: if paper stays available, staff will default to it. Samir agreed the habit is the main risk.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Nadia Brooks** — revise the prototype with larger touch targets by next Tuesday; add a high contrast theme to the backlog.\n- **Elif Kaya** — recruit five front-desk staff for usability tests in three weeks.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Elif prefers morning meetings, before clinic hours.\n- Samir is back to nearly full hours.\n"
  },
